.git
.parity
runtime
node_modules
**/node_modules
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
packages/account/data
packages/data/data
packages/history/data
packages/ota/data

# Deployment state and credentials must never be baked into an image, even if
# an operator accidentally creates them outside the two primary data mounts.
# Do not ignore every directory named `data`: packages/data is a runtime
# service, not deployment state. The two host data roots above are ignored in
# full, while these patterns catch common state files in other locations.
**/data/*.json
**/data/*.db
**/data/*.sqlite
**/data/*.sqlite3
**/*.bak
**/*.backup
**/*.log
**/*.tgz
**/*.tar
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/*credentials*.json
**/*secrets*.json
**/*store*.json
**/member-photos
**/classic-media
**/classic-backups
**/classic-keys
**/classic-logs

# Source-control metadata, local test receipts, and optional compiled profiles
# are not runtime inputs and can contain sensitive or unreviewed material.
.parity
docs/parity/evidence
runtime
